From: Noa Himesaka <himesaka@noa.codes>
Subject: [PATCH] media: iris: allow larger capture buffer pools on HFI Gen1

Threaded VA-API clients such as VLC can hold more than 32 decoded
surfaces before they hand them back. The default vb2 limit of 32
buffers keeps them from allocating the capture pool they ask for.

Raise the HFI Gen1 decoder CAPTURE queue limit to
DEFAULT_MAX_HOST_BUF_COUNT (64). This only raises the maximum userspace
may request; the minimum allocation, the OUTPUT queue and the encoder
are unchanged. The firmware is still told the same BUFFER_COUNT_ACTUAL
values as before; in split mode the host-facing OUTPUT2 count is the DPB
count, which is already below the 32 buffers the host may queue today.
More than 32 queued buffers has not been tested on Gen1 firmware.

This is the HFI Gen1 counterpart of the gen2 patch carried by
qcom-va-driver ("media: iris: allow larger capture buffer pools on HFI
gen2").

Signed-off-by: Noa Himesaka <himesaka@noa.codes>
Assisted-by: Claude:claude-opus-5-5
---
 drivers/media/platform/qcom/iris/iris_vidc.c |    3 +++
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/media/platform/qcom/iris/iris_vidc.c b/drivers/media/platform/qcom/iris/iris_vidc.c
index bc95f75..ee44718 100644
--- a/drivers/media/platform/qcom/iris/iris_vidc.c
+++ b/drivers/media/platform/qcom/iris/iris_vidc.c
@@ -122,6 +122,9 @@ iris_m2m_queue_init(void *priv, struct vb2_queue *src_vq, struct vb2_queue *dst_
 	dst_vq->drv_priv = inst;
 	dst_vq->buf_struct_size = sizeof(struct iris_buffer);
 	dst_vq->min_reqbufs_allocation = MIN_BUFFERS;
+	if (inst->domain == DECODER &&
+	    inst->core->iris_firmware_data == &iris_hfi_gen1_data)
+		dst_vq->max_num_buffers = DEFAULT_MAX_HOST_BUF_COUNT;
 	dst_vq->dev = inst->core->dev;
 	dst_vq->lock = &inst->ctx_q_lock;
 
